// REQUIRES: long
// P03.25 (ADR-0025, CLAUDE.md lessons): the unit analysis stays near-linear:
// a chain of 10,000 units; the factor limit; the parser depth limit. The input
// is generated (Inputs/gen-units-stress.py) and checked within a CPU-time
// ceiling of three times its cost alone, counted in units of `gopp version`
// (tests/cpu-limit.py; the growth is
// judged by the near-linear checks); nothing
// nests deeper than the parser allows and no walk is
// recursive over the size of the input.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-stress.py chain 10000 > %t.chain.gopp
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 16 30 -- %gopp check %t.chain.gopp
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-stress.py overflow 5000 > %t.over.gopp
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 400 310 --status 1 -- %gopp check %t.over.gopp 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVER
// OVER: error[E0435]: unit factor out of range: unit U4096: the factor is no longer an exact rational (it needs more than 4096 bits)
// OVER-NOT: error[E
// Parentheses nest only as deep as the parser allows: an error, not a crash.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-stress.py nest 10000 > %t.nest.gopp
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 4 4 --status 1 -- %gopp check %t.nest.gopp 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NEST
// NEST: error[E0030]: exceeded max nesting depth
// A ring of 10,000 units: one error that lists every member (found by the
// iterative walk), the same with one body thread and with eight, and nothing
// more for a unit that depends on the ring; the ring is near-linear up to
// 160000 (Inputs/check-linear.py: 10000 and 160000, at most 48 times the CPU
// time). The factor limit and the parser's depth limit bound the other two.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-stress.py ring 10000 > %t.ring.gopp
// RUN: not timeout 240 %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ring.gopp > %t.ring.out 2>&1
// RUN: not timeout 240 %gopp check -check-j=8 --check-error-limit=0 %t.ring.gopp > %t.ring.8 2>&1
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-linear.py --label ring --out %t.ringlin --n 160000 --status 1 --gen "%S/Inputs/gen-units-stress.py ring {n}" -- %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 {file}
// RUN: diff %t.ring.out %t.ring.8
// RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=RINGTEXT %s < %t.ring.out
// RUN: grep -c 'error\[E' %t.ring.out | FileCheck --check-prefix=RING %s
// RINGTEXT: error[E0422]: unit cycle: R0 -> R1 -> R2 -> R3
// RINGTEXT-SAME: -> R9999 -> R0 (UNI-3)
// RING: 1
// Near-linear: the shape at N and at 4N, the larger run at most 12 times the
// smaller (a quadratic analysis takes 16 times; Inputs/check-units-linear.py).
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-units-linear.py --gopp %gopp --gen %S/Inputs/gen-units-stress.py --out %t.lin chain 10000 | FileCheck --check-prefix=LIN-CHAIN %s
// LIN-CHAIN: chain: near-linear yes
